  "plausible_answers": [
    "Answer A (Physical Therapy Default): Start with a structured physical therapy program \u2014 for most chronic knee conditions, PT produces outcomes equivalent to surgery without the risk, recovery time, or cost.",
    "Answer B (Surgery for Structural Damage): Proceed to surgery if imaging confirms significant structural damage (complete ACL tear, severe OA, locked meniscus) \u2014 PT cannot repair structural deficits and delaying surgery risks further joint deterioration.",
    "Answer C (PT Then Reassess): Complete a full 8\u201312 week PT course then reassess with imaging \u2014 this approach exhausts conservative treatment, provides documented PT failure if surgery is later needed, and avoids unnecessary procedures."
